# Harness maintenance

## When this applies

Whenever you **add or materially change** durable documentation under:

- `docs/` (except transient scratch),
- `automation/docs/`,
- or cross-references / new paths under `.cursor/` (including `.cursor/pipelines/` and **MCP** guidance in `.cursor/HOW-TO.md` when postgres-ctqa or `mcp.json` layout changes),

you must **in the same change** (or an immediate follow-up) update:

- [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) — “Where things live” and any pointers that agents rely on.
- [README.md](README.md) — quick links if a new top-level artifact matters to humans.
- [docs/harness-map.json](docs/harness-map.json) — tiers, keyword packages, or `read` paths if discovery behavior changes.
- Any affected [.cursor/rules/](.cursor/rules/) or [.cursor/prompts/](.cursor/prompts/) files.

Goal: **no orphan references** and no drift between “what exists” and “what the harness says.”

## Content policy (summaries)

Updates to [docs/project.json](docs/project.json), [docs/qa-project.json](docs/qa-project.json), or process blurbs in AGENTS/README/rules must stay **functional and process-oriented**:

- **Do not** add individual names, PM/BA/QA rosters, or ownership contact lists.
- **Do not** copy **passwords, tokens, or secrets** from Confluence or Jira into the repository; point to authenticated sources instead.
